From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: hjviewer <haejin.cho@yonsei.ac.kr>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 02:08:48 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 102/167] hjviewer: review fixes, session1 lane (1.9)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

TV-W7, a switch that arrives late: when the old page's close ends past the
10 s limit but before the limit's timer (or after a resume from the
background), pageClosed() now says it is late and hjvSessionPageClosed
gives the toast (filesFailed / remoteFailed) and cancels the timer, instead
of dropping the switch silently. A test covers the case.

TV-W7, W7-D10 "no dialog open": the first guide also waits while a route is
above the remote page or a dialogManager dialog or the app lock is open.
Those are overlay entries, not routes (common.dart's show() inserts an
OverlayEntry), so ModalRoute.isCurrent alone does not see them; each holds a
back interceptor while open, the only ones the app adds, so the check reads
BackButtonInterceptor.describe(). The Wayland prompt condition stays. No
common.dart change.

TV-W7, F1's guest line: logged in counts a stored access_token as
hjviewer_access.dart's _loggedIn() does, so a phone whose user name has not
loaded yet is not told to enter the 이용 비밀번호 again.

TV-W7, the connection token: the new page takes it once from the switch
(hjvSessionTakeToken in initState) and no longer keeps it on the widget;
connect() goes back to the 1.8.2 code (no connToken on the phone pages).

TV-W7 nits: F1 names the file screen's button by its tooltip ("원격 화면으로
바꾸기" / "Switch to the remote screen") and where it is; the gesture panel
opened by hand on an Android peer leaves out the three-finger scroll row.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
